windowcast links third-party crates under licences compatible with the
GPL-3.0. The protocol-layer crates a backend is built on are listed here;
every other dependency's licence is in its own crate (`cargo tree`).

IronRDP (ironrdp and its ironrdp-* crates)
  https://github.com/Devolutions/IronRDP
  Authors: Devolutions Inc., Teleport and the IronRDP contributors.
  Dual-licensed under the MIT licence or the Apache License, version 2.0;
  windowcast uses it under the MIT licence.

sspi (sspi-rs), used by IronRDP for CredSSP/NLA
  https://github.com/Devolutions/sspi-rs
  Authors: Devolutions Inc. and the sspi-rs contributors.
  Dual-licensed under the MIT licence or the Apache License, version 2.0;
  windowcast uses it under the MIT licence.

winscard (Devolutions sspi-rs workspace), used by sspi for smart cards
  https://github.com/Devolutions/sspi-rs
  Authors: Devolutions Inc. and contributors.
  Dual-licensed under the MIT licence or the Apache License, version 2.0;
  windowcast uses it under the MIT licence.

Patched copies: vendor/ironrdp-connector (0.10.0), vendor/sspi (0.21.3)
and vendor/winscard (0.3.4) are those crates as published, with only
their picky (and, for sspi, macOS/iOS RustCrypto) requirements moved to
picky 7.0.0-rc.27's, so they build beside russh; each has a
README.windowcast.md saying exactly what changed and why. They go once
upstream releases on picky rc.27 or later.

